<p><strong>Seeking Green light</strong>: Yes<br />
<strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP article<br />
<strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong>A photo album that can predict disasters and death.<br />
<strong>Central Narrative:</strong> A long explanation of how the photo album works. It shows photos of a woman in various places, from various time periods. Depending on how long the viewer has to live, the woman will appear to be a different age. The places she appears in the photos are sites of famous disasters shortly before they happened, such as 9/11 or Chernobyl. The article ends with the writer speculating they could use the book to predict containment breaches or disasterous experiments by having their personnel look at the book, but then there's an addendum. A new photo has appeared in the book, and the background is the SCP site it's being held in.<br />
<strong>Hook:</strong> Through the course of the story, the book seems relatively harmless (if a little disturbing) but some things, like the name of the site it's held at, are redacted for unclear reasons. Then at the end, why it was redacted becomes clear, and it raises whole new questions about the true nature of the book and the future.<br />
<strong>Additional notes:</strong> This might be more a question for full draft editing, but I'm not sure whether to spice it up with more speculations or hints about how dangerous the book actually is, or whether to keep it more passive or mysterious. (Adding notes from one researcher to another, test logs, etc.)</p>

